== Third-party components: ggml (MIT) ==

Quantised block formats and HIP kernels under third_party/ggml and
kernels/src/ggml_*.hip.

- third_party/ggml/ is a verbatim, unedited snapshot of a subset of the ggml
  sources shipped in https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp (the `ggml/`
  directory plus the repository-root LICENSE), pinned at commit
  2e0d86bebc210947680e8f0d67daa79f3260c106 (2026-10-28). The pin, the
  upstream path of every file and its SHA-256 are recorded in
  third_party/ggml/PIN; any local change lives as a patch file under
  third_party/ggml-patches/, never inside the snapshot.
  Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors. Licensed MIT; the copyright
  notice and permission notice are retained in third_party/ggml/LICENSE
  (verbatim) and in every imported file. The imported files keep their
  upstream terms (MIT) and are NOT relabelled Apache-2.0; they are excluded
  from scripts/governance/apply_spdx_headers.py (any `third_party/` path).

- kernels/src/ggml_*.hip are hipfire shim files (SPDX `Apache-2.0`) derived
  from ggml: they #include the pinned upstream headers and loop or call
  upstream's device functions (`vec_dot_*_q8_1` of the mmvq shims,
  `dequantize_*` of ggml_convert_shim.hip, whose gather and dequantise kernel
  bodies are transcriptions of upstream's convert.cu / getrows.cu kernels), and
  carry a "Derived from ggml (MIT)" line. Each compiled shim object
  (kernels/ggml_*_shim_gfx1201.co) contains code compiled from both.

hipfire imports ggml's quantised-weight formats and kernels (MIT) as a
library for GGUF-native serving; it is not a wrapper around llama.cpp: the
executor, attention/GDN/MoE/KV/speculation, dispatch and the PeaceMaker
toolchain are hipfire's.

